One important thing I'd change before you use this on the entire project

The current DTO detector:

name.endsWith("dto")
|| name.endsWith("request")
|| name.endsWith("response")
|| name.endsWith("model")

is intentionally simple. In a real microservice codebase, this can accidentally classify classes such as:

PaymentModel
DatabaseModel
SomeResponse

as DTOs.

Since your goal is finding DTOs that can actually be commoned out, I would make the next version detect:

@Data

@Getter / @Setter

@JsonProperty

@JsonIgnore

Java record

DTO/request/response package

fields

inheritance

nested DTOs


and, importantly, produce a "Commonization Candidate" score rather than treating every 80% structural match as something that should definitely be commonized.

That would make the report much more useful for deciding which DTOs you should actually move into your common library.